Design: AI trading pipeline (1H XAU/USD)
1. High-level flow

Data ingestion — load hourly OHLCV.

Cleaning — resample/fill missing, timezone fix.

Feature engineering — indicators, returns, price patterns, context (DXY).

Labeling — define target (binary/multi) with forward horizon & threshold.

Train/validate — use time-aware splits + walk-forward (rolling).

Modeling — XGBoost / LightGBM as baseline; LSTM/CNN later.

Thresholding & calibration — convert probabilities to trade signals.

Backtesting — realistic execution, slippage, spreads, fees, position sizing.

Paper trading / Live — connect to broker API for signals/execution.

Monitoring — P&L, drawdown, model drift; retrain schedule.

2. Data & preprocessing

Required columns: datetime, open, high, low, close, volume (index = datetime).

Ensure uniform hourly spacing: df = df.asfreq('1H') then interpolate() or forward-fill small gaps.

Remove daylight time issues (use UTC).

Example:

import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_csv("gold_data.csv", index_col=0, parse_dates=True)
df = df.sort_index()
df = df.tz_localize(None).asfreq("1H")
df = df.fillna(method="ffill")  # small gaps OK; for long gaps drop

3. Feature engineering (core set)

Create features that capture momentum, trend, volatility, and structure.

Basic price features

returns: r1 = close.pct_change()

log returns

Trend / MAs

EMA fast/slow: 12, 26, 50, 200

SMA 20, 50

Momentum

RSI(14)

Stochastic %K/%D

Volatility

ATR(14)

rolling std of returns (window 20)

Mean reversion / bands

Bollinger Bands (20,2): bb_high, bb_low, bb_pct = (close - bb_mid)/(bb_high-bb_low)

Price action & structure

previous candle body size, upper/lower wick ratios

HH/LL breakout flags vs n-period high/low (n=24,48)

Context

DXY (USD index), US10Y, VIX (if available) aligned to same frequency

Time features

hour of day, day of week, is_market_open (some FX/commodity seasonality)

Use ta or pandas to compute.

Example snippet:

